---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About" description="Who writes Truth-Poly and why." />
		<style>
			main {
				text-align: left;
			}
			.notice {
				padding: 1em;
				border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
				background: rgb(var(--gray-light));
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p>
				I'm Mia. I'm interested in world events and markets, and I want a career in market making
				and trading. In the meantime I trade prediction markets on Polymarket.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Truth-Poly</strong> is the automated trading pipeline I built for my technology
				project. The code is on
				<a href="https://github.com/miagavin/truth-poly-ise">GitHub</a>.
			</p>
						<h2>What's next</h2>
			<p>
				I want to keep developing Truth-Poly. I'd like to try MCP servers so the AI can take full
				control of placing the Polymarket trade, and a more sophisticated model than Claude Haiku.
				Because the AI has to be tested rigorously against edge cases, that takes careful work.
			</p>
			<h2>What you'll find here</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="/blog">Blog</a>: how each part of the pipeline works.</li>
				<li><a href="/trades">My Trades</a>: a public log of trades, with the numbers.</li>
			</ul>
			<p class="notice">
				<strong>Not financial advice.</strong> This is a personal project and a learning log.
				Prediction markets can lose you money; never risk more than you can afford to lose.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html> 